@node gpui-builder Manual
@chapter Crate @code{gpui-builder}
@cindex gpui-builder
@cindex layout solver

@code{gpui-builder} is a generic, constraint-based layout solver used
by the SotF desktop player to handle resizable panels, collapsible
sidebars and aspect-driven axis switching. The core solver is
framework-agnostic; only the optional @code{showcase} feature pulls in
GPUI.

@menu
* gpui-builder User Guide::
* gpui-builder Developer Guide::
@end menu

@node gpui-builder User Guide
@section User Guide

End users experience the solver as:

@itemize @bullet
@item Sidebars that collapse when the window narrows.
@item Panels that flip from horizontal to vertical layout based on
  aspect ratio.
@item Draggable dividers that remember their position via user
  preferences.
@item Smooth handling of headers, footers and toolbars that should not
  shrink.
@end itemize

@node gpui-builder Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading Sizing model

@table @code
@item Sizing::Fixed
Hard constraint. Headers, footers, toolbars.
@item Sizing::Fractional
Soft constraint with target ratio and minimum.
@item Sizing::Flex
Pure flex: takes whatever is left.
@end table

@subheading Behaviour knobs

@itemize @bullet
@item Priority-based collapse: lowest-priority slots collapse first.
@item Auto-axis switching: container flips H/V based on aspect ratio.
@item Display tiers: slots report active mode (e.g.@: Full vs Mini)
  based on resolved size.
@item User preferences: ratio overrides and manual collapse state.
@item Text-measured sizing: slots can be sized by text content via
  the @code{TextMeasure} trait (from @ref{gpui-pretext Manual}).
@end itemize

@subheading Quick example

@example
let children = [
    LayoutNode::Slot(SlotNode @{
        id: "sidebar",
        sizing: Sizing::fractional(0.2, 120.0),
        priority: 0.5,
        collapsible: true,
        display_tiers: &[],
        collapse_label: Some("Sidebar"),
        @dots{}
    @}),
    @dots{}
];
let solved = solve(/* @dots{} */);
@end example

@subheading Showcase binary

@example
cargo run -p gpui-builder --features showcase
@end example

@subheading Testing

The solver has dense unit-test coverage; run with
@code{cargo test -p gpui-builder}.
